From e8c7bce089b518b5d9076d585ebc469e9c390ff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Schaller <cschalle@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:56:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] media: i2c: imx471: Fix test pattern register width

TEST_PATTERN_MODE at 0x0600 is a 16 bit register, but the driver
declares it with CCI_REG8. An 8 bit write only reaches the high byte, so
selecting a pattern writes the mode number into 0x0600 while 0x0601
stays zero, leaving the register at mode * 256 and the sensor producing
no pattern at all.

Every other 16 bit register in this driver is already declared with
CCI_REG16 (0x0202 exposure, 0x0204 analogue gain, 0x0340 FLL, 0x020e
digital gain); 0x0600 is the only one that is not.

The control was accepted and read back correctly while having no effect:
with V4L2_CID_TEST_PATTERN set to 2 ("Eight Vertical Colour Bars"),
either before streaming or while streaming, captured frames still showed
the live scene with an unchanged horizontal profile.

Fixes: be1589e567ae ("media: i2c: imx471: Add Sony IMX471 image sensor driver")
Signed-off-by: Christian Schaller <cschalle@redhat.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
index 348dbd3de..2db1b05b5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
 #define IMX471_REG_ORIENTATION			CCI_REG8(0x0101)
 
 /* Test Pattern Control */
-#define IMX471_REG_TEST_PATTERN			CCI_REG8(0x0600)
+#define IMX471_REG_TEST_PATTERN			CCI_REG16(0x0600)
 
 /* default link frequency and external clock */
 #define IMX471_LINK_FREQ_DEFAULT		200000000LL
-- 
2.55.0

